{
  "_about": [
    "admin1-capitals.json — the seat of each unit of admin1-spec.json, with the seat's coordinate AS FETCHED from Wikidata (P625 of the city item named by the unit's P36 statement), for the capitals' dot table of the map cards (build-card-faces.js, the `india-states` layer) and the seats check of check-admin1.js.",
    "Retrieved 2026-11-14 from query.wikidata.org: SELECT ?unit ?iso ?cap ?coord WHERE { ?unit wdt:P300 ?iso . FILTER(STRSTARTS(?iso, \"IN-\")) ?unit p:P36 ?st . ?st ps:P36 ?cap . OPTIONAL { ?cap wdt:P625 ?coord } }. Never typed from memory.",
    "Where a unit has two P36 statements the card plan's choice is taken and the other named in `also` (docs/india-geography-card-plan.md \"The capitals\"): Jammu and Kashmir — Srinagar (summer) over Jammu (winter); Ladakh — Leh over Kargil; Karnataka — Bengaluru over Belagavi (the second legislature seat); Maharashtra — Mumbai over Nagpur (the winter session); Uttarakhand — Dehradun over Gairsain (named the summer capital in 2020); Madhya Pradesh — Bhopal (Nagpur's statement ended in 1956).",
    "`name` is the card plan's name for the seat (Sri Vijaya Puram for Wikidata's 'Srivijayapuram'; Puducherry for the city Wikidata labels 'Pondicherry'); `qid` the city item. `inUnit`: the seat lies in ANOTHER unit by fact — Chandigarh is the capital of Punjab and of Haryana and a union territory of its own (the plan's gin-516 and gin-518)."
  ],
